From 58f3282c3edaab7122f02c21a2b9e605c58675df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 03:46:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: add Elastic Common Schema JSON output

Add -logformat=json-ecs with @timestamp, log.level, log.logger, process.thread.name, log.origin fields, ecs.version=8.11.0 and event.action. Use typed registry ECS names and prefix custom fields with lotus. Convert durations to the integer nanoseconds required by event.duration; generic formats keep microseconds. Retain the required ECS event timestamp even when text timestamps are disabled.

Checked names and units against the ECS 8.11 references. All 33 logging/event cases pass, including typed values, source metadata, custom namespace and nanosecond units. feature_logging validates actual startup/mining/shutdown file output with timestamps disabled. Elasticsearch and external collector ingestion have not been run.

(cherry picked from commit 84850a5a31f2ab494e30201ba6a2008c04e10db9)

N3-Source-Commit: 84850a5a31f2ab494e30201ba6a2008c04e10db9
N3-Source-Export: 0025

Nonfinite JSON format coverage: extend existing raw F64 test to JsonGcpEncoder and JsonEcsEncoder only after both classes exist here and the earlier encoder fix is folded. No production tail conversion or new FLOAT producer key. Original native20case590assertion controls source-scoped; final209 runtime pending. Source fixup03a38e59; transport f46f3bf5d7c5d7a3ee49ac3bff7454cabbb2bcf9.
